import sys
p = sys.argv[1]
lines = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| 651 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1
lines.insert(idx[0] + 1, "| 652 | 2026-10-24 | **Scales take what the Lesson Book's major scale chapter says and they did not (her question 14:06, 'nothing more from the Lesson Book in Scales?').** Built on row 651; no new lessons and no new steps, only lines and one picture inside the lessons as they are. (1) The same pattern from any note: the book's 'each letter once' ('So the 7th note is F♯, a whole step from E. Not G♭: a scale uses every letter once.'; F major: 'Not A♯: every letter once.'). (2) White keys: the book's 'thumb under / 3 over': right hand 'Finger 5 is on top. Coming down, 3 crosses over the thumb.', left hand 'Then 3 crosses over the thumb: fingers 3, 2, 1.' (3) The degrees: 'Every note of the scale has a number and a name. 8 is 1 again, an octave higher.' (4) All twelve keys: its whole picture is now the book's keyboard clock (the cover of the major scale chapter, 'Turned, C major's shape starts on any key'), in the book's frame; tap a key and the same shape turns to start there (it plays that note); One by one and Your turn are as before. (5) The Home's line for Black keys, left hand, in the lesson's order: 'One shape for D♭, E♭, A♭ and B♭.' (6) Korean: 샵나 → 샵이나, app-wide (21 places, books and workbooks included). **Left as they are (structure):** the book's check-up page (My five checks) and the definition of a scale on its cover ('notes in order, step by step, to the same letter an octave away'); the 'At the piano' steps stay out (row 650). Files: drills.html, drills.src.html, _workspace/concept-book-kit/sc/patch676.py. |")
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(lines)); print('ok')
